& [PruningTrace] removes scope bleed while preserving lineage
  + PRUNE-001 vintage Simula syntax compatibility -> outside; process semantics survive in a Cantor-native profile
  + PRUNE-002 direct Simula-to-FPGA claim -> false_identity; replace with canonical IR plus separately proved backend
  + PRUNE-003 one monolithic runtime-procedure-hardware signature -> scope_bleed; split three authority grades
  + PRUNE-004 arbitrary model-created executable procedures -> unsafe; preserve candidate authorship followed by separate phase receipts
  + PRUNE-005 self-signing or self-admitting generated code -> prohibited authority collapse
  + PRUNE-006 direct mid-forward hidden-state injection -> unsupported; preserve explicit stop-tool-result-later-pass protocol
  + PRUNE-007 shared mutable attention across models -> false transport identity; preserve messages and negotiated frames
  + PRUNE-008 silence or timeout as consensus -> unsafe; preserve typed incomplete and timeout states
  + PRUNE-009 consensus as truth -> semantic overclaim; preserve agreement as one evidence-bearing protocol outcome
  + PRUNE-010 native FPGA as first backend -> premature optimization; preserve software interpreter reference first
  + PRUNE-011 choosing SystemVerilog, VHDL, HLS, CIRCT, vendor, board, or device now -> unsupported target commitment
  + PRUNE-012 model-generated HDL loaded directly -> unsafe device authority collapse
  + PRUNE-013 live calendar, provider, clock, notifications, Git, database, filesystem, or network -> outside first deterministic proof
  + PRUNE-014 production persistence and concurrency -> outside; preserve explicit immutable state API for later profiles
  + PRUNE-015 general SOP compiler claim from one fixture -> overclaim; retain bounded correspondence fixture only
  + PRUNE-016 arbitrary dynamic objects, inheritance, recursion, reflection, and native coroutine capture -> unbounded or opaque
  + PRUNE-017 neural weights as the SOP association store -> false current necessity; preserve inspectable graph and deterministic procedure records
  + PRUNE-018 hardware speed as proof of semantic accuracy -> invalid inference; preserve independent semantic proof
  + PRUNE-019 one-letter or acronym-heavy language syntax design -> premature aesthetics; retain semantic forms first
  + PRUNE-020 direct procedure access to the entire SOP catalogue -> scope_bleed; retain pinned declared anchor set

& [QuarantinedAlternatives] remain available for later evidence
  + a bytecode virtual machine may replace or complement tree-walk IR interpretation after measurement
  + WASM may be a portable software backend after effect and determinism mapping
  + CIRCT Handshake may be a hardware compiler IR after target proof
  + a soft processor may execute procedure bytecode on FPGA when flexibility justifies area and latency
  + native FPGA kernels may use HLS or generated RTL after profiling
  + persistent catalogue and distributed controller may follow the effectless in-memory experiment
  + live model-provider adapters may follow a provider-neutral tool schema proof

& [SurvivingArchitecture] is minimal but complete
  + deterministic CTPR state transition library over proved forms
  + effectless Cantor Process Procedure source profile
  + canonical typed Cantor Process IR
  + deterministic software interpreter as the first executable reference
  + separate validation, compilation, verification, admission, catalogue, invocation, and revocation receipts
  + explicit message-based multi-pass shared inference and token-ring stability experiment
  + non-executable FPGA eligibility and correspondence profile
  + later interpreter and native hardware realization options

& [GrowthSeedSet] is grounded and deferred
  + GROW-001 concrete Cantor Process Procedure textual syntax after machine forms and IR semantics prove stable
  + GROW-002 provider-neutral JSON tool schemas after procedure invocation forms stabilize
  + GROW-003 persistent signed catalogue after in-memory lifecycle and revocation proof
  + GROW-004 live provider and calendar profiles after effect authorization and privacy design
  + GROW-005 distributed message transport after single-process deterministic session replay
  + GROW-006 performance profiling to identify real FPGA-eligible kernels
  + GROW-007 target-specific FPGA addendum covering toolchain, device, side channels, secure boot, loading, and rollback
  + GROW-008 property verification and model checking for scheduler, ring, barrier, and resource bounds
  + GROW-009 stable semantic anchor query tool integration after catalogue and authority proofs
  + GROW-010 procedure-learning candidates after authorship, admission, revocation, and evaluation histories exist

& [PruningDisposition] is stable
  + the surviving architecture advances the user's intended shared semantic inference junction without pretending that model or hardware boundaries have disappeared
  + further current growth should deepen proof mappings rather than add new runtime features
